### Undergraduate West Lafayette — Introductory & Core CS Courses
CS 10100 — Digital Literacy — Fabrizio Cicala  
CS 15900 — C Programming — John Robinson, Ning Zhou, Eman Samy Diyab, William N. Crum  
CS 17600 — Data Engineering in Python — Xiaojin Liu  
CS 17700 — Programming With Multimedia Objects — Jessica Mackey Conner-Strunk, Marta A. Crowe  
CS 18000 — Problem Solving and Object-Oriented Programming — Tony Bergstrom, Jeffrey A. Turkstra  
CS 18200 — Foundations of Computer Science — Anuran Makur  
CS 19000-SC1 — Intro to Professional Practice — Jermaine Williams, Jr  
CS 19300 — Tools — Paula C. Ramos Perez, Ryan H. Sierra, Pranavi Chaganti, Hanako S. Keney, Jagannath Prabhakaran  

_________________________

### Undergraduate West Lafayette — Systems, Algorithms, and DS/AI Foundations
CS 21100 — Competitive Programming I — Ethan Dickey  
CS 24000 — Programming In C — Christopher K. May  
CS 24200 — Introduction To Data Science — Tony Bergstrom, Caitlin Whitter  
CS 24300 — Artificial Intelligence Basics — Yexiang Xue  
CS 25000 — Computer Architecture — George B. Adams III  
CS 25100 — Data Structures And Algorithms — Jeremiah M. Blocki, Michael H. Borkowski  
CS 25200 — Systems Programming — Christopher K. May, Gustavo A. J. Rodriguez-Rivera  
CS 25300 — Data Structures And Algorithms For DS/AI — Konstantinos Ameranis  
CS 29100-LE1 — Soph Developmt Seminar — John R. Langenkamp  

_________________________

### Undergraduate West Lafayette — Upper-Level CS Electives
CS 30700 — Software Engineering I — Jeffrey A. Turkstra  
CS 31100 — Competitive Programming II — Arvind Ramaswami  
CS 31400 — Numerical Methods — Alex Pothen  
CS 33400 — Fundamentals Of Computer Graphics — Voicu S. Popescu  
CS 34800 — Information Systems — Hisham R. Benotman  
CS 35200 — Compilers: Principles And Practice — Changhee Jung  
CS 35400 — Operating Systems — Douglas E. Comer  
CS 35500 — Introduction To Cryptography — Hemanta K. Maji  
CS 36100 — Great Issues In Computer Science — Gustavo A. J. Rodriguez-Rivera  

_________________________

### Undergraduate West Lafayette — AI, ML, Data, Security, Robotics, HCI, Theory, Capstone
