University Catalog Overview
The Purdue University Catalog provides essential information for current and prospective students, including details on academic programs, policies, and resources. It features a selection of catalogs from various academic years, allowing users to access historical data and course offerings. The catalog is organized into sections for easy navigation, including general information, undergraduate and graduate programs, and academic regulations.
__________________________________________________
Course Information: CS 18000
**Course Title:** CS 18000 - Problem Solving And Object-Oriented Programming  
**Credit Hours:** 4.00  
**Description:** This course focuses on problem-solving and algorithms, implementing algorithms in a high-level programming language, conditionals, iterative approaches, debugging, data collections, searching and sorting, problem decomposition, object-oriented programming, subclassing, exception handling, graphical user interfaces (GUIs), file data storage, abstract data types, and an overview of topics from other computer science courses. It is primarily intended for students majoring in computer sciences.  
**Restrictions:** Credit cannot be obtained for both CS 18000 and any of CS 15600, CS 15800, or CS 15900. Not open to students with credit in CS 24000.  
**Availability:** Typically offered in Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters.  
**Credits:** 4.00
