Department of Computer Science Overview
The Department of Computer Science at Purdue University provides a comprehensive overview of its resources and facilities. It includes information about the various computing facilities available to members of the department, including access to UNIX machines and email servers for authorized individuals from remote locations. The department supports nine undergraduate computing labs, while Purdue Information Technology (Purdue IT) maintains a range of research and instructional laboratories available to CS members.
__________________________________________________
Purdue IT Facilities
Purdue Information Technology operates the Rosen Center for Academic Computing (RCAC), now known as Research Computing. This center features several large clusters of computers, including the Bell Cluster, Gilbreth GPU Cluster, Halstead Cluster, and Scholar Instructional Cluster, which are utilized by research faculty across campus. Additionally, RCAC manages extensive storage and archival systems, including the Data Depot and Fortress Archive.
__________________________________________________
Purdue Libraries and Research Repository
Purdue Libraries maintains the Purdue University Research Repository, an online collaborative workspace and data-sharing platform designed to support the data management needs of Purdue researchers and their collaborators. This repository facilitates the organization and sharing of research data, enhancing collaboration and accessibility.
__________________________________________________
Emergency Support and Plans
The document mentions emergency support and plans related to the Department of Computer Science facilities, including the DSAI Emergency Plan and LWSN Emergency Plan. These plans are designed to ensure the safety and security of individuals using the facilities and outline procedures to follow in case of emergencies.
