================WEBPAGE: 2357=================

WEBPAGE: www.stat.purdue.edu_resources_facilities.htm

Computing Facilities Overview
The Department of Statistics at Purdue University collaborates with the College of Science (Science IT) and the central university computing group (Purdue IT) to provide comprehensive computing facilities and support. These resources include instructional labs, classroom technologies, core network infrastructure, and research computing, ensuring a robust environment for world-class instruction and research.
__________________________________________________
IT Staff and Departmental Facilities
The Department of Statistics is supported by a centralized IT organization within the College of Science. It maintains a variety of Linux servers and workstations, both physical and virtual, for research and administrative tasks. The servers operate on the Ubuntu operating system and vary in power, featuring configurations with 8 to 28 CPU cores. Notably, the department has servers with up to 1TB of RAM and various storage capacities, including a maximum of 168TB on the largest server.
__________________________________________________
University Computing Resources
Purdue IT offers extensive computing resources, including supercomputers with 1-3PB of dedicated scratch storage, over 15 petabytes of automated tape storage, and a 3 petabyte on-demand storage facility. The campus is equipped with high-speed connectivity, featuring at least 20 Gbps links between buildings and a 200 Gbps connection to the national research network. The university regularly updates its supercomputers, which often rank among the fastest globally.
__________________________________________________
Rosen Center for Advanced Computing (RCAC)
The Rosen Center for Advanced Computing (RCAC) provides various research computing solutions, including the Community Cluster Program, which pools resources from grants and faculty to fund supercomputers. RCAC manages these systems, allowing researchers to focus on their work without the burden of system management.
__________________________________________________
Additional Resources and Support
The Department of Statistics offers various resources, including a tutor list, emergency plans, help room hours, and internal communication tools. These resources are designed to support students and faculty in their academic and administrative needs.
__________________________________________________
Contact Information
Purdue Department of Statistics  
150 N. University St, West Lafayette, IN 47907  
Phone: (765) 494-6030  
Fax: (765) 494-0558
__________________________________________________
