WEBPAGE: rcac.purdue.edu_index.php_compute_hammer

Data Depot V3 Storage Migration Announcement
Purdue University is conducting a migration of the Data Depot V3 storage system, which will take place from October 29, 2025, at 11:00 AM to December 31, 2025, at 12:00 AM EST. This migration is part of ongoing efforts to enhance data storage capabilities for users.
__________________________________________________
Overview of Hammer
Hammer is a high-throughput computing resource optimized for Purdue's communities, particularly those utilizing loosely-coupled computing. Initially built in partnership with HP and Intel in April 2015, Hammer has undergone expansions, with annual updates planned to keep nodes in production for five years from their initial purchase. Users interested in accessing Hammer can purchase access via the Cluster Access Purchase page and are encouraged to subscribe to the Community Cluster Program Mailing List for updates.
__________________________________________________
Hammer Specifications
The Hammer computing resource consists of multiple nodes with identical hardware configurations. Each node features varying numbers of processor cores and Ethernet interconnects. The specifications include:
- **Front-Ends**: 2 nodes with Two Haswell CPUs @ 2.60GHz, 20 cores, 64 GB memory, retiring in 2020.
- **Sub-Clusters**: 
  - A: 198 nodes, Two Haswell CPUs @ 2.60GHz, 20 cores, 64 GB memory, retiring in 2020.
  - B: 40 nodes, Two Haswell CPUs @ 2.60GHz, 40 logical cores, 128 GB memory, retiring in 2021.
  - C: 27 nodes, Two Sky Lake CPUs @ 2.60GHz, 48 logical cores, 192 GB memory, retiring in 2022.
  - D: 18 nodes, Two Sky Lake CPUs @ 2.60GHz, 48 logical cores, 192 GB memory, retiring in 2023.
  - E: 15 nodes, Two Intel Xeon Gold CPUs @ 2.60GHz, 48 logical cores, 96 GB memory, retiring in 2024.
All nodes run Rocky 8 and utilize Slurm for job management.
__________________________________________________
Hammer Usage and Management
Hammer nodes allow for unlimited stack usage and core dump size, although disk space and server quotas may still apply. Users can load the recommended compiler and libraries by executing `$ module load rcac` and verify loaded modules with `$ module list`. The system is maintained with security patches as needed.
__________________________________________________
Purdue University Contact Information
Purdue University is located at 610 Purdue Mall, West Lafayette, IN 47906. For inquiries, users can contact the university at 765-494-4600.
__________________________________________________

