Final Answer:
To access Purdue University's High-Performance Computing (HPC) resources, follow these steps:  1.
**Submit a Request**: You must submit a service request through the "Purdue IT Request" button
available on the HPC portal. This is the primary method for accessing HPC services and getting your
inquiries addressed.  2. **RCAC Service Request**: For specific service requests, use the RCAC
(Research Computing and Analytics Center) Service Request form, which allows you to direct questions
and requests to the support team.  3. **Account Setup**: If you are new to using HPC resources, you
will need to request an account. When doing so, be sure to specify your research group, such as the
"Mathematics Department" if applicable.  4. **Accessing Clusters**: For larger computational tasks,
depending on your needs, you can connect to various clusters such as Gilbreth (for GPU-intensive
applications) or Hammer (optimized for high-throughput computing).  5. **User Guides**: Familiarize
yourself with user guides available for different HPC resources to understand account setup, file
storage, software usage, and job running procedures.  If you encounter any issues, you can report
