The schedule for CS34800: Information Systems in Spring 2026, outlines various topics and important
dates throughout the semester. Here's a summary of the schedule:  ### Key Dates and Topics:  ####
Week 1: - **West Lafayette**: Classes begin January 13, 2026. - **Indianapolis**: Classes begin
January 12, 2026. - Topics: Introduction to relational databases and SQL.  #### Week 2: - No class
on January 19, 2026 (MLK Day). - Topics include SQL fundamentals, joins, set operators, and
subqueries.  #### Week 3: - Homework assignments related to advanced SQL.  #### Week 4: - Focus on
relational algebra.  #### Week 5: - Discuss storage and indexing, with continued SQL education.
#### Week 6: - Topics: Database design and use cases, with a project stage assigned.  #### Week 7: -
Explore the ER model and normalization.  #### Week 8: - Contents include functional dependencies and
storage.  #### Week 9: - **Midterm Exam 1 on March 10, 2026**, at 8:00 PM.  #### Week 10: - No
classes for Spring Break (March 17 & 19, 2026).  #### Week 11: - Introduces NoSQL and database
technologies.  #### Week 12: - Further discussions on NoSQL databases.  #### Week 13: - Topics on
transactions and isolation.  #### Week 14: - Focus on analytical databases.  #### Week 15: - Discuss
distributed databases.  #### Week 16: - **Midterm Exam 2 on April 27, 2026**, at 8:00 PM.  ###
Important Notes: - No final exam is scheduled. - Homework assignments and project stages will have
specific due dates highlighted in the course materials.  For complete weekly details, follow the
detailed outlines available on the course schedule link provided in the syllabus. Always refer to
the [Course Schedule](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1mov5_UbuG9F6wt_QZWm8yGn4kfpkYqokqkzzgk
0kwOU/edit?usp=sharing) for updates and specifics on readings and assignments.
