Final Answer:
Here is the information I can provide for CS44000 (Large-scale Data Analytics) based on the context
given:  ### Course Information - **Course Title:** Large-scale Data Analytics - **Semester:** Spring
2026 - **Instructor:** Jianguo Wang     - **Email:**
[csjgwang@purdue.edu](mailto:csjgwang@purdue.edu) (please include "[CS440]" in the subject line)
### Course Description The course covers key concepts, design principles, and systems to analyze
large-scale data to extract transformative insights, focusing on big data techniques.  ### Tentative
Topics - Database fundamentals - Big data storage (e.g., HDFS) - Big data computing frameworks
(e.g., Hadoop, Spark) - Data warehouses and data lakes - Graph analytics (e.g., Spark Graph) - Data
streaming (e.g., Spark Streaming) - Large-scale machine learning (e.g., Spark MLlib) - Vector
databases - Cloud-native data analytics  ### Class Logistics - **When:** Mondays and Wednesdays,
3:30 PM - 4:20 PM - **Where:** Wilmeth Active Learning Center 3087 - **Office Hours:** After class
or by appointment - **Pre-requisites:** CS242, CS251, and CS373  ### Labs and PSOs - Labs will start
from the 3rd week of the semester. - **Lab Schedule:**   - L01: Tuesday 1:30 PM - 3:20 PM (LWSN
B131)   - L02: Friday 9:30 AM - 11:20 AM (LWSN B131)   - L03: Wednesday 9:30 AM - 11:20 AM (LWSN
B131)   - L04: Wednesday 11:30 AM - 1:20 PM (LWSN B131)  ### Online Communications - **Piazza** will
be used for announcements, discussions, and Q&A. Brightspace will be utilized only for occasional
emails. **Gradescope** will be for homework submissions and grading.  ### Textbooks (Optional) -
*Spark: The Definitive Guide* by Bill Chambers and Matei Zaharia - *Database System Concepts* (7th
edition) by Avi Silberschatz, Henry F. Korth, and S. Sudarshan - *Mining of Massive Datasets* by
Jure Leskovec, Anand Rajaraman, and Jeff Ullman  ### Grading Breakdown - Homeworks: 20% (2 * 10%) -
Midterm Exam: 25% - Final Exam: 35% - Project: 20% (2 * 10%) - Extra Credits: 5%  ### Course
Schedule Highlights - **Lec 1:** Course Introduction (01/12) - **Lec 3:** No class (MLK Day, 01/19)
- **Lec 4:** No class (Conference Trip, 01/21) - **Lec 16:** Midterm Exam (03/04) - **Lec 19 & 20:**
No class (Spring Break, 03/16 & 03/18) - **Lec 32:** Review (04/29)  ### Teaching Assistants -
**Shige Liu:** [liu3529@purdue.edu](mailto:liu3529@purdue.edu) - **Yunan Zhang:**
[zhan4404@purdue.edu](mailto:zhan4404@purdue.edu) - **Jiayi Liu:**
[liu4127@purdue.edu](mailto:liu4127@purdue.edu)  If you need additional specific information, please
feel free to ask! Be cautious about any additional details not provided in this context, as there
may be a risk of hallucination without proper sources.
