When deciding on a Computer Science track, consider the following options based on your interests
and career goals:  1. **Core Computer Science Track**:    - Focuses on fundamental concepts of
computer science.    - Includes courses like CS 18000 (Problem Solving and Object-Oriented
Programming), CS 18200 (Foundations of Computer Science), and CS 25100 (Data Structures and
Algorithms).  2. **Machine Intelligence Concentration**:    - Ideal if you're interested in Data
Mining, Machine Learning, or Artificial Intelligence.    - Core courses include CS 37300 (Data
Mining and Machine Learning) and CS 47300 (Web Information Search).  3. **Data Science Track**:    -
If you want to combine statistics and computer science for data analytics roles.    - Core courses
include CS 24200 (Introduction to Data Science), STAT 35500 (Statistics for Data Science), and CS
37300.  4. **Software Engineering Focus**:    - Suitable for careers in software development and
project management.    - Courses like CS 30700 (Software Engineering I) and CS 40800 (Software
Testing) would be beneficial.  5. **Specialized Electives**:    - You may choose from electives
based on your interests in areas like cybersecurity, cloud computing, or artificial intelligence.
Consider how these tracks align with your personal interests and career aspirations. Discussing your
options with an academic advisor can provide tailored advice based on your academic progress and
goals.
