  - SQL in programming languages
  - SQL injection vulnerabilities
- **Assignments**: 
  - Homework 2 due
  - Homework 3 assigned
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Sections 5.1, 9.1, 9.2, 9.4.1–9.4.3, 9.6

---

#### Week 6 — Database Design
- **West Lafayette**: February 17 & 19, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: February 16 & 18, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - Database design
  - Use cases
  - Entity-Relationship (ER) model
- **Assignments**: 
  - Project Stage 2 assigned
  - Homework 3 due on February 21, 2026
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Sections 6.1–6.7, 6.9–6.10

---

#### Week 7 — ER Model, Functional Dependencies, Normalization
- **West Lafayette**: February 24 & 26, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: February 23 & 25, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - ER model
  - Functional dependencies
  - Database normalization
- **Assignments**: 
  - Homework 4 assigned
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Sections 7.1–7.4.1, 7.8–7.9

---

#### Week 8 — Storage and Indexing
- **West Lafayette**: March 3 & 5, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: March 2 & 4, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - Functional dependencies and normalization (continued)
  - Storage and indexing
- **Assignments**: 
  - Homework 4 due
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Section 12.1, Sections 14.1–14.2.2, 14.2.4–14.2.5, Section 14.3 (excluding 14.3.3 and 14.3.4), Sections 14.5–14.7

---

#### Week 9 — Midterm Examination
- **West Lafayette**: March 10 & 12, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: March 9 & 11, 2026
- **Schedule**:
  - Monday: No lecture
  - Tuesday, March 10, 2026 — Midterm Exam 1, 8:00 PM – 9:30 PM
    - Locations: 
      - West Lafayette: PHYS 112 and PHYS 114
      - Indianapolis: ES 2107
