================WEBPAGE: 6066=================
---

CS348 Spring 2026 Calendar: This is the schedule for CS348 spring 2026. 

### Important Notes
- This schedule is preliminary and subject to change.
- Some schedule text may be clipped in spreadsheet views; ensure full visibility when referencing original tables.
- The course does not have a final exam.
- Two evening midterm exams will be held.

---

### Course Schedule

#### Week 1 — Introduction to Relational Databases
- **West Lafayette**: January 13, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: January 12, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - Course logistics
  - Relational data model
  - Introduction to SQL
- **Assignments**: Project Stage 1 assigned
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Sections 1.1–1.3, 1.8, 1.9
  - Sections 2.1–2.4
  - Sections 3.1–3.4 (excluding 3.2.2)

#### Week 1 (continued) — SQL Aggregations
- **West Lafayette**: January 15, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: January 14, 2026
- **Topics**: SQL aggregations

---

#### Week 2 — SQL Fundamentals
- **West Lafayette**: January 20 & 22, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: January 19 & 21, 2026
- **Special Date**: MLK Day — No Class on January 19, 2026
- **Topics**:
  - SQL joins
  - Set operators
  - SQL subqueries
- **Assignments**: 
  - Project Stage 1 due
  - Homework 1 assigned
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Sections 4.1, 3.5, 3.6, 3.7, 3.8 (excluding 3.8.8)

---

#### Week 3 — Advanced SQL
- **West Lafayette**: January 27 & 29, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: January 26 & 28, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - SQL views
  - NULL values
  - Updates
  - Stored procedures
  - Triggers
- **Assignments**: 
  - Homework 1 due
  - Homework 2 assigned
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Sections 4.2, 5.2, 5.3, 3.9

---

#### Week 4 — Relational Algebra
- **West Lafayette**: February 3 & 5, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: February 2 & 4, 2026
- **Topics**: Relational Algebra
- **Recommended Reading**: Section 2.6

---

#### Week 5 — Cloud Databases and SQL Security
- **West Lafayette**: February 10 & 12, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: February 9 & 11, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - Relational Algebra (continued)
  - Databases in the Cloud (Google Cloud Platform)
  - SQL in programming languages
  - SQL injection vulnerabilities
- **Assignments**: 
  - Homework 2 due
  - Homework 3 assigned
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Sections 5.1, 9.1, 9.2, 9.4.1–9.4.3, 9.6

---

#### Week 6 — Database Design
- **West Lafayette**: February 17 & 19, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: February 16 & 18, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - Database design
  - Use cases
  - Entity-Relationship (ER) model
- **Assignments**: 
  - Project Stage 2 assigned
  - Homework 3 due on February 21, 2026
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Sections 6.1–6.7, 6.9–6.10

---

#### Week 7 — ER Model, Functional Dependencies, Normalization
- **West Lafayette**: February 24 & 26, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: February 23 & 25, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - ER model
  - Functional dependencies
  - Database normalization
- **Assignments**: 
  - Homework 4 assigned
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Sections 7.1–7.4.1, 7.8–7.9

---

#### Week 8 — Storage and Indexing
- **West Lafayette**: March 3 & 5, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: March 2 & 4, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - Functional dependencies and normalization (continued)
  - Storage and indexing
- **Assignments**: 
  - Homework 4 due
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Section 12.1, Sections 14.1–14.2.2, 14.2.4–14.2.5, Section 14.3 (excluding 14.3.3 and 14.3.4), Sections 14.5–14.7

---

#### Week 9 — Midterm Examination
- **West Lafayette**: March 10 & 12, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: March 9 & 11, 2026
- **Schedule**:
  - Monday: No lecture
  - Tuesday, March 10, 2026 — Midterm Exam 1, 8:00 PM – 9:30 PM
    - Locations: 
      - West Lafayette: PHYS 112 and PHYS 114
      - Indianapolis: ES 2107
  - Wednesday: Asynchronous online lecture (Topic: Storage and indexing)

---

#### Week 10 — Spring Break
- **West Lafayette**: March 17 & 19, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: March 16 & 18, 2026
- **Note**: No classes

---

#### Week 11 — Storage, Indexing, and NoSQL
- **West Lafayette**: March 24 & 26, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: March 23 & 25, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - Storage and indexing
  - NoSQL and Big Data
  - Introduction to Neo4j
- **Assignments**: 
  - Homework 5 assigned
  - Project Stage 2 due on March 28, 2026
  - Project Stage 3 assigned
- **Resources**: Neo4j Developer Guides: [Neo4j Developer](https://neo4j.com/developer/cypher-query-language/#learn-cypher)

---

#### Week 12 — NoSQL Databases
- **West Lafayette**: March 31 & April 2, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: March 30 & April 1, 2026
- **Topics**: 
  - Neo4j
  - MongoDB
- **Resources**: MongoDB Documentation: [MongoDB Docs](https://docs.mongodb.com/manual/)

---

#### Week 13 — Transactions and Isolation
- **West Lafayette**: April 7 & 9, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: April 6 & 8, 2026
- **Topics**:
  - MongoDB (continued)
  - ACID properties
  - Transactions
  - Isolation levels
- **Assignments**: 
  - Homework 5 due
  - Homework 6 released
- **Recommended Reading**: 
  - Chapter 17 (excluding 17.7 and 17.9), Sections 18.1–18.1.3

---

#### Week 14 — Analytical Databases
- **West Lafayette**: April 14 & 16, 2026
- **Indianapolis**: April 13 & 15, 2026
- **Topics**:
