model: ### CS 34800: Information Systems Overview

**Course Information:**
- **Title:** CS 34800: Information Systems
- **Credit Hours:** 3
- **Prerequisites:** Data Structures, Discrete Structures, and programming experience.

**Course Description:**
CS 34800 covers fundamental concepts of database management, primarily focusing on the relational model. Key topics include:
- Schema design and refinement
- Query languages
- Database application development
- Transactions and concurrency control
- Overview of NoSQL databases (including graph and document stores)
- Overview of OLAP and data warehousing

**Lectures:**
- **Meeting Times:**
  - Indianapolis: **MW 5:30 PM to 6:45 PM**
  - West Lafayette: **TuTh 10:30 AM to 11:45 AM**

**Homework and Projects:**
- Six graded homework assignments and one individual application project will be assigned.
- Late homework is accepted within 72 hours with a penalty.

**Examinations:**
- Two midterm exams (open-book and open-note) will be conducted.

**Grading Breakdown:**
- Assignments: 10%
- Brightspace Quizzes: 2%
- In-class Participation: 3%
- Lab Exam (SQL): 20%
- 1st Midterm Exam: 25%
- 2nd Midterm Exam: 30%
- Web/Mobile Application Project: 10%

**Communication:**
- Questions should be posted on Ed for quicker responses; emails should be reserved for sensitive issues.

For detailed schedules, resources, and updates, refer to the course materials on Brightspace.

This summary provides an overview of the important elements in the CS 34800 course for Spring 2026. If you have any specific questions or need more details, feel free to ask!

